      "problem": "John bought $25$ candies for $$3.$ What is the price per candy?",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of dollars to candies is $3:25.$ Expressing this as a fraction, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{25}\n$$\n\nWe can convert this fraction to a decimal by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 4}{25\\times 4}=\\frac{12}{100}=0.12\n$$\n\nConsequently, the cost is $$0.12$ per candy.",
